      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "The winning run of NO NOTTHEBUTTONS (1) came to an end last week but there was still plenty of merit in his effort to lead from wider and fight well to go under narrowly. Won his lone try at this longer distance and has the speed to take advantage of the ace draw. JORGE STREET (4) has been racing well against stronger company and put the writing on the wall when beaten 3m into second in the Vic Frost at Listed level here last start. Goes well at this longer distance and looks suited in this line-up. BETTER ECLIPSE (3) has been solid from wide barriers of late so will enjoy the lower draw. RAVISHING SLOY (5) is hard to knock having come from wider to win his last two outings here. Go well again along with DESSIE GEE (6) who draws wider but deserves respect off the last-start win.",
